# AICL Example: MLOps Platform
# Comprehensive MLOps platform covering experiment tracking, model registry, CI/CD for ML,
# model monitoring, and automated retraining with full lifecycle management.

Goal Build a production MLOps platform that provides end-to-end ML lifecycle management including experiment tracking, model registry with governance, CI/CD pipelines for ML, real-time model monitoring, and automated retraining triggered by performance degradation

Constraint All models must pass governance review before production deployment
Constraint Experiment tracking must capture all parameters, metrics, and artifacts for full reproducibility
Constraint CI/CD pipelines must validate model performance, fairness, and security before deployment
Constraint Model monitoring must detect performance degradation within 15 minutes of onset
Constraint Automated retraining must not deploy without human approval for production-critical models

Risk Experiment tracking data loss causing irreproducible results
Recovery Implement multi-region replicated artifact storage; maintain write-ahead log for experiment metadata; enable point-in-time recovery from backups; validate artifact integrity on retrieval

Risk Model registry corruption from concurrent registration conflicts
Recovery Implement optimistic locking on model version registration; deploy transactional registration with rollback; maintain audit trail of all registry mutations; enable recovery from registry snapshots

Risk CI/CD pipeline deploying biased or unsafe model to production
Recovery Implement mandatory fairness and safety gates in pipeline; deploy canary validation with automated rollback; require human approval gate before full deployment; enforce policy-as-code checks

Risk Model monitoring blind spot missing gradual performance degradation
Recovery Deploy multi-signal monitoring with statistical process control; implement sliding window analysis with adaptive thresholds; use ensemble of drift detection methods; require periodical manual review

Risk Automated retraining producing worse model than current production
Recovery Implement champion-challenger comparison before any deployment; require automated evaluation to beat current model on all metrics; maintain rollback capability to previous champion; log all retraining decisions

Risk Infrastructure cost overrun from uncontrolled retraining jobs
Recovery Implement cost budgets per project with hard limits; prioritize retraining jobs by business impact; use spot instances for training; enforce resource quotas and time limits on jobs

Layer ExperimentTracking
    SubLayer: ParameterLogging
    SubLayer: MetricCollection
    SubLayer: ArtifactStorage
Layer ModelRegistry
    SubLayer: VersionManagement
    SubLayer: GovernanceReview
    SubLayer: ArtifactSigning
Layer CICD
    SubLayer: PipelineOrchestration
    SubLayer: ValidationGates
    SubLayer: DeploymentAutomation
Layer Monitoring
    SubLayer: PerformanceMonitoring
    SubLayer: DriftDetection
    SubLayer: AlertManagement
Layer Retraining
    SubLayer: TriggerEvaluation
    SubLayer: TrainingOrchestration
    SubLayer: ChampionChallenger

Validation All experiment parameters and metrics must be captured within 1 second of logging
Validation Model registration must enforce uniqueness of model name and version combination
Validation CI/CD pipeline must complete validation within 2 hours for standard models
Validation Model monitoring must detect 5% accuracy degradation within 15 minutes
Validation Automated retraining must achieve equal or better metrics than current production model
Validation Governance review must complete within 24 hours of submission
Validation Artifact integrity must be verified via checksum on every retrieval
Validation Cost alerts must trigger within 5 minutes of budget threshold breach

# Level 2 - Entities

Entity Experiment
    experimentId: string
    experimentName: string
    projectName: string
    parameters: dict
    metrics: dict
    artifactUris: list
    tags: list
    status: string
    startTime: datetime
    endTime: datetime
    createdBy: string
    parentId: string

Entity ModelRegistration
    registrationId: string
    modelName: string
    modelVersion: string
    framework: string
    artifactUri: string
    artifactChecksum: string
    signatureUri: string
    experimentId: string
    governanceStatus: string
    registeredAt: datetime
    registeredBy: string
    description: string

Entity CICDPipeline
    pipelineId: string
    pipelineName: string
    modelTarget: string
    stages: list
    validationGates: list
    approvalRequirements: list
    rollbackConfig: dict
    lastRunId: string
    status: string
    createdAt: datetime

Entity MonitoringAlert
    alertId: string
    modelId: string
    alertType: string
    severity: string
    metricName: string
    currentValue: float
    thresholdValue: float
    detectionTime: datetime
    status: string
    assignedTo: string
    remediationAction: string

Entity RetrainingJob
    jobId: string
    modelId: string
    triggerReason: string
    datasetVersion: string
    hyperparameters: dict
    trainingMetrics: dict
    evaluationMetrics: dict
    challengerStatus: string
    submittedAt: datetime
    completedAt: datetime
    costUsd: float

Entity GovernanceReview
    reviewId: string
    modelRegistrationId: string
    reviewer: string
    reviewStatus: string
    fairnessReport: dict
    securityReport: dict
    performanceReport: dict
    approvalConditions: list
    submittedAt: datetime
    reviewedAt: datetime
    comments: string

# Level 3 - Behaviors

Behavior TrackExperiment
    Input:
        experimentConfig: dict
        parameters: dict
        metrics: dict
        artifacts: list
    Output:
        experiment: Experiment
        trackingReport: dict
    Action:
        Create experiment entry with unique identifier
        Log all hyperparameters with type validation
        Record metrics with timestamps for time-series analysis
        Store artifact references with checksum verification
        Link to parent experiment if specified
        Emit ExperimentCreated event for tracking

Behavior RegisterModel
    Input:
        modelArtifact: dict
        metadata: dict
        governanceConfig: dict
    Output:
        registration: ModelRegistration
        governanceReview: GovernanceReview
    Action:
        Validate model artifact integrity via checksum
        Check model name and version uniqueness in registry
        Compute model signature from input/output schema
        Submit model for governance review
        Create registration entry with pending governance status
        Emit ModelRegistered event for pipeline integration

Behavior ExecuteCICDPipeline
    Input:
        pipeline: CICDPipeline
        modelRegistration: ModelRegistration
        executionConfig: dict
    Output:
        pipelineResult: dict
        deploymentDecision: dict
    Action:
        Validate model passes all pre-deployment checks
        Run unit tests on model serving code
        Execute integration tests against staging environment
        Run fairness and bias evaluation gates
        Run security scanning on model artifact
        Evaluate canary deployment metrics
        Generate deployment decision with evidence
        Emit PipelineCompleted event

Behavior MonitorModelPerformance
    Input:
        modelId: string
        monitoringConfig: dict
    Output:
        performanceReport: dict
        alerts: list
    Action:
        Collect real-time inference metrics from serving endpoint
        Compute rolling accuracy, latency, and error rate metrics
        Apply statistical process control for anomaly detection
        Compare current metrics against baseline thresholds
        Generate alerts for any threshold violations
        Compute feature drift metrics on input distributions
        Return performance report with alert list

Behavior TriggerRetraining
    Input:
        modelId: string
        triggerReason: string
        retrainingConfig: dict
    Output:
        retrainingJob: RetrainingJob
        approvalRequest: dict
    Action:
        Evaluate trigger reason and severity
        Fetch latest approved training dataset version
        Configure hyperparameters from retraining policy
        Submit retraining job to training orchestrator
        Schedule champion-challenger evaluation upon completion
        Request human approval if model is production-critical
        Emit RetrainingTriggered event for tracking

Behavior ConductGovernanceReview
    Input:
        modelRegistration: ModelRegistration
        reviewConfig: dict
    Output:
        governanceReview: GovernanceReview
        approvalDecision: dict
    Action:
        Generate fairness report across protected attributes
        Run security scan on model artifact and dependencies
        Validate performance meets minimum thresholds
        Check compliance with model risk tier requirements
        Assign reviewer based on model risk classification
        Compile approval decision with conditions
        Emit GovernanceReviewCompleted event

# Level 4 - Conditions

Condition: PerformanceDegradationDetected
    When model accuracy drops more than 5% from baseline over 1-hour window
    Then trigger monitoring alert; initiate retraining evaluation; activate shadow deployment of backup model; alert model owner

Condition: GovernanceReviewExpired
    When governance review remains pending for more than 48 hours
    Then escalate to governance lead; block model deployment; notify model owner and reviewer; flag for compliance audit

Condition: CICDPipelineFailure
    When any pipeline validation gate fails
    Then halt deployment immediately; generate failure report with root cause; notify pipeline owner; block subsequent deployments until issue resolved

Condition: RetrainingBudgetExceeded
    When cumulative retraining cost exceeds project budget allocation
    Then pause all pending retraining jobs; alert project owner; require budget approval to resume; prioritize critical retraining only

Condition: ArtifactIntegrityViolation
    When artifact checksum verification fails during retrieval
    Then block artifact usage immediately; alert security team; quarantine artifact; initiate integrity investigation; fall back to last verified version

# Level 5 - Events

Event: ExperimentCreated
    On new experiment logged in tracking system
    Action: index experiment for search; notify project dashboard; validate parameter completeness; link to project hierarchy

Event: ModelRegistered
    On model artifact registered in model registry
    Action: initiate governance review; trigger CI/CD pipeline; update model catalog; notify stakeholders

Event: GovernanceReviewCompleted
    On governance review decision rendered
    Action: update model registration status; notify model owner of decision; if approved, enable deployment; if rejected, document remediation steps

Event: DeploymentCompleted
    On model successfully deployed through CI/CD pipeline
    Action: activate monitoring; initialize baseline metrics; notify operations team; update deployment dashboard; archive previous model version

Event: MonitoringAlertTriggered
    On model monitoring detecting threshold violation
    Action: create alert with severity classification; notify on-call team; evaluate auto-remediation options; log alert for post-incident review

Event: RetrainingCompleted
    On automated retraining job finishing
    Action: evaluate challenger vs champion; generate comparison report; request deployment approval; update retraining metrics dashboard

# Level 6 - Concurrency

Parallel:
    Multiple experiment tracking writes from concurrent training runs
    Model registration alongside governance review processing
    CI/CD pipeline stages with independent validation gates
    Performance monitoring across multiple deployed models
    Retraining job execution with monitoring
    Artifact integrity verification concurrent with retrieval

# Level 7 - Optimization

Optimize: Experiment tracking write throughput
    Priority: Asynchronous metric logging with batching; compressed artifact storage; partitioned tracking database by project

Optimize: CI/CD pipeline execution time
    Priority: Parallelize independent validation gates; cache test datasets; incremental testing based on changed components only

Optimize: Model monitoring cost efficiency
    Priority: Sample-based monitoring with adaptive sampling rates; aggregate metrics before storage; tiered retention with downsampling

# Level 8 - Learning

Learn: Optimal monitoring thresholds per model
    Goal: Set detection thresholds that catch real degradation while minimizing false alerts
    Adapt: Alert thresholds and detection window parameters per model
    Based: Historical alert accuracy, missed detections, and false positive rates

Learn: Retraining trigger policy optimization
    Goal: Retrain models at optimal frequency to maintain performance without wasting resources
    Adapt: Retraining trigger conditions, cooldown periods, and dataset selection
    Based: Degradation patterns, retraining outcomes, and cost-benefit analysis

Learn: CI/CD pipeline stage optimization
    Goal: Minimize pipeline execution time while maintaining validation quality
    Adapt: Stage ordering, parallelization strategy, and test selection
    Based: Historical pipeline execution times, failure patterns, and stage dependencies

Learn: Governance review prioritization
    Goal: Prioritize reviews for highest-risk models while maintaining SLA for all reviews
    Adapt: Review queue ordering and reviewer assignment
    Based: Model risk classification, business impact, and review SLA compliance history

# Level 9 - Security

Security:
    Encrypt: All model artifacts and experiment data at rest using AES-256 with envelope encryption
    Encrypt: API communication with mutual TLS 1.3 and OAuth2 Bearer token authentication
    Protect: Model registry from unauthorized modifications via signed artifact verification and RBAC
    Protect: Experiment tracking data with project-scoped access controls
    Encrypt: CI/CD pipeline secrets and deployment credentials with vault integration
    Protect: Monitoring alert data from tampering via append-only audit logging
    Protect: Governance review decisions with digital signature from authorized reviewers

# Level 10 - Native

Native: python
{
import hashlib
import json
from datetime import datetime, timedelta
from typing import Dict, List, Optional, Tuple
from dataclasses import dataclass, field
from collections import defaultdict

@dataclass
class ExperimentTracker:
    experiments: Dict[str, Dict] = field(default_factory=dict)

    def log_experiment(self, name: str, params: Dict, metrics: Dict,
                       artifacts: List[str], project: str = "default",
                       parent_id: Optional[str] = None) -> Dict:
        exp_id = hashlib.sha256(
            f"{name}:{datetime.utcnow().isoformat()}".encode()
        ).hexdigest()[:16]

        experiment = {
            "experiment_id": exp_id,
            "experiment_name": name,
            "project_name": project,
            "parameters": params,
            "metrics": metrics,
            "artifact_uris": artifacts,
            "tags": [],
            "status": "running",
            "start_time": datetime.utcnow().isoformat(),
            "end_time": None,
            "created_by": "system",
            "parent_id": parent_id
        }
        self.experiments[exp_id] = experiment
        return experiment

    def log_metric(self, experiment_id: str, metric_name: str,
                   value: float, step: int = 0) -> None:
        if experiment_id in self.experiments:
            exp = self.experiments[experiment_id]
            if "metric_history" not in exp:
                exp["metric_history"] = defaultdict(list)
            exp["metric_history"][metric_name].append({
                "value": value,
                "step": step,
                "timestamp": datetime.utcnow().isoformat()
            })

@dataclass
class ModelRegistry:
    models: Dict[str, List[Dict]] = field(default_factory=dict)

    def register(self, name: str, version: str, artifact_uri: str,
                 framework: str, experiment_id: str,
                 description: str = "") -> Tuple[Dict, bool]:
        if name not in self.models:
            self.models[name] = []

        existing_versions = [m["version"] for m in self.models[name]]
        if version in existing_versions:
            return {"error": f"Version {version} already exists for {name}"}, False

        checksum = hashlib.sha256(artifact_uri.encode()).hexdigest()

        registration = {
            "registration_id": hashlib.sha256(
                f"{name}:{version}".encode()
            ).hexdigest()[:16],
            "model_name": name,
            "model_version": version,
            "framework": framework,
            "artifact_uri": artifact_uri,
            "artifact_checksum": checksum,
            "experiment_id": experiment_id,
            "governance_status": "pending",
            "registered_at": datetime.utcnow().isoformat(),
            "description": description
        }
        self.models[name].append(registration)
        return registration, True

    def get_model(self, name: str, version: str) -> Optional[Dict]:
        versions = self.models.get(name, [])
        for m in versions:
            if m["model_version"] == version:
                return m
        return None

    def list_versions(self, name: str) -> List[Dict]:
        return self.models.get(name, [])

@dataclass
class PerformanceMonitor:
    baselines: Dict[str, Dict] = field(default_factory=dict)
    alert_history: List[Dict] = field(default_factory=list)
    degradation_threshold_pct: float = 5.0
    evaluation_window_minutes: int = 60

    def set_baseline(self, model_id: str, metrics: Dict) -> None:
        self.baselines[model_id] = {
            "metrics": metrics,
            "set_at": datetime.utcnow().isoformat()
        }

    def evaluate(self, model_id: str, current_metrics: Dict) -> Dict:
        baseline = self.baselines.get(model_id)
        if not baseline:
            return {"status": "no_baseline", "model_id": model_id}

        alerts = []
        baseline_metrics = baseline["metrics"]
        for metric_name, baseline_value in baseline_metrics.items():
            if metric_name not in current_metrics:
                continue
            current_value = current_metrics[metric_name]
            if baseline_value != 0:
                pct_change = ((current_value - baseline_value) / abs(baseline_value)) * 100
            else:
                pct_change = 0.0

            if pct_change < -self.degradation_threshold_pct:
                alert = {
                    "model_id": model_id,
                    "metric_name": metric_name,
                    "baseline_value": baseline_value,
                    "current_value": current_value,
                    "pct_change": pct_change,
                    "severity": "high" if pct_change < -10 else "medium",
                    "detected_at": datetime.utcnow().isoformat()
                }
                alerts.append(alert)
                self.alert_history.append(alert)

        return {
            "model_id": model_id,
            "alerts": alerts,
            "degradation_detected": len(alerts) > 0
        }

@dataclass
class ChampionChallenger:
    champion: Optional[Dict] = None
    challenger: Optional[Dict] = None
    minimum_improvement_pct: float = 1.0

    def evaluate_challenger(self, challenger_metrics: Dict) -> Dict:
        if not self.champion:
            self.challenger = challenger_metrics
            return {"decision": "promote", "reason": "no_existing_champion"}

        champion_score = self.champion.get("primary_metric", 0)
        challenger_score = challenger_metrics.get("primary_metric", 0)

        if champion_score != 0:
            improvement = ((challenger_score - champion_score) / abs(champion_score)) * 100
        else:
            improvement = 100.0 if challenger_score > 0 else 0.0

        if improvement >= self.minimum_improvement_pct:
            self.challenger = challenger_metrics
            return {
                "decision": "promote",
                "improvement_pct": improvement,
                "champion_score": champion_score,
                "challenger_score": challenger_score
            }
        return {
            "decision": "reject",
            "improvement_pct": improvement,
            "reason": f"Improvement {improvement:.2f}% below minimum {self.minimum_improvement_pct}%"
        }
}
